---
import Base from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL || '/';
---

<Base title="Terms & Conditions — Compliance365" description="Website terms of use for Compliance365.">
  <Header />

  <section class="container section">
    <div class="card" style="padding:22px;border-radius:14px">
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="muted small">Last updated: October 2025</p>

      <h2>1. About this website</h2>
      <p>
        This website (<strong>Site</strong>) is operated by Compliance365 Pty Ltd (<strong>we</strong>, <strong>our</strong>, <strong>us</strong>).
        By using the Site, you agree to these Terms &amp; Conditions (<strong>Terms</strong>).
        If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Content on the Site is general information only and is not legal, risk, security or compliance advice.
        You should obtain independent advice for your circumstances.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the Site lawfully and not in a way that disrupts others’ use.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt to gain unauthorised access or introduce malware.</li>
        <li>Provide accurate details when submitting forms or enquiries.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our handling of personal information is set out in our <a href={base + 'privacy'}>Privacy Policy</a>.
        We work <strong>within your environment</strong> for client engagements and do not store your organisation’s
        sensitive data in our systems, unless expressly agreed in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Unless stated otherwise, we own or license all IP in the Site (text, graphics, logos, code and materials).
        You must not reproduce, adapt or commercialise any content without our prior written consent.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Third-party tools &amp; links</h2>
      <p>
        The Site may link to third-party sites or embed third-party tools (e.g. scheduling, analytics).
        We are not responsible for their content or practices. Your use of third-party services is at your own risk
        and may be subject to their terms.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Availability &amp; changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may change, suspend or discontinue any part of the Site without notice. We do not guarantee
        that the Site will be available, secure or error-free at all times.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law (including the Australian Consumer Law), we exclude all warranties,
        representations and guarantees not expressly set out in these Terms. Our liability for any claim connected
        with the Site is limited to re-supplying the relevant service or the cost of doing so. We are not liable for
        indirect or consequential loss, loss of profit, data, goodwill or opportunity.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        You indemnify us against losses, claims, costs or liabilities arising from your breach of these Terms or
        misuse of the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Cookies &amp; Consent</h2>
      <p>
        We use essential and analytical cookies. You can manage preferences via <a href={base + 'cookies'}>Cookie Settings</a>.
        For details see our <a href={base + 'privacy'}>Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of Queensland, Australia. You submit to the non-exclusive jurisdiction
        of the courts of Queensland and the Commonwealth of Australia.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions? Email <a href="mailto:info@compliance365.com.au">info@compliance365.com.au</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>
